题）\r\n**12** Distance Matrices（距离矩阵）\r\n> <span style=color:#1e8449;>**[note] 译者注（OCR 修正）：** 末尾三行的编号在 OCR 中作 `皿 10`、`The 0 感 ho gonal Pro crustes P roblem`、`D istance Matrices`：`皿` 为章号标记的残损、`0 感 ho gonal Pro crustes` 还原为 Orthogonal Procrustes；此三章延续 IV.1–IV.7 的章号序列，故记为 10、11、12。本批正文仅覆盖 IV.1–IV.7。\r\n−-- OCR 原文 −--\r\nIV.I\r\nIV,2\r\nIV.3\r\nIV,4\r\nIVS\r\nlV.6\r\nlV•7\r\nlV•8\r\nPart IV\r\nSpecial Matrices\r\nFourier Transforms ： Discrete and Continuous\r\nShift Matrices and Circulant Matrices\r\nTh e Kronecker P ro duct A ． B\r\nS ine and Cosine Transforms from Kronecker Sums\r\nToeplitz Matrices and Shift lnvariant ilters\r\nGraphs and L aplacians and Kirchhoff's Laws\r\nCIustering by SpectraI Metho ds and k-means\r\n皿 10\r\nCompleting Rank 0 ne Matrices\r\nThe 0 感 ho gonal Pro crustes P roblem\r\nD istance Matrices\r\n\r\n########## page_205（书页 203）｜Part IV 介绍（Special Matrices）\r\n−-- 译文（待审）---\r\n<!-- page 205 −->\r\n> <span style=color:#7f8c8d;>本页为书页 203，是 Part IV（Special Matrices，特殊矩阵）的章首导言页；页眉与页脚印页码为重复元素，不译、不收录。\r\n<span style=color:#2471a3;>**[section]**\r\n## Part IV：Special Matrices（特殊矩阵）\r\n> <span style=color:#1e8449;>**[note] 译者注（OCR 修正）：** 本页 OCR 噪声极重，按数学语境重建如下：`Founer` → Fourier（傅里叶）；`砀 “ r 忉 巳` → shift invariance（平移不变性）；`co “ 况` → convolution（卷积）；`孝 产` → filter（滤波器）；`山` → With；`0 n` → often；`fimte` → finite；`iS enormou &` → is enormous；`sto of CNN ， s` → story of CNN's；`CI “ s ca 五 0 视` → Classification；`Deep Co “ 况 Neural e ks` → Deep Convolutional Neural Networks；`蓋` → $A$（关联矩阵）；`baphlical` → graphical；`posiUve` → positive。\r\n本章展开两个宏大的主题：Discrete Fourier Transforms（离散傅里叶变换）所需的关键矩阵，以及 graphical models（图模型）所需的关键矩阵。\r\n当问题具有特殊的结构时，这两个主题都会出现在机器学习之中——而这种结构正体现在神经网络的架构（architecture）里。\r\nFourier（傅里叶）对应的是具有 shift invariance（平移不变性）的问题。\r\n对图像中某一个像素所做的运算，与对下一个像素所做的运算是同一个运算。\r\n在这种情形下，该运算就是一次 convolution（卷积）。\r\n底层矩阵的每一行都是上一行的移位，每一列都是上一列的移位。\r\nConvolutional nets（卷积网络）在每个像素周围使用同一组 weights（权重）。\r\n有了这种 shift-invariant（平移不变）的结构，convolution matrix（卷积矩阵，在图像处理中称为 filter，滤波器）就具有 constant diagonals（常数对角线）。\r\n在一维问题中，$n \\times n$ 矩阵完全由它的第一行与第一列决定。\r\n很多时候该矩阵是 banded（带状的）——因为 filter（滤波器）具有 finite length（有限长度）——于是它在某一条对角线带之外全为零。\r\n对于由重复的一维分块构成的二维问题，这种节省是巨大的。\r\n这使得我们能够使用 Convolutional Neural Net（卷积神经网络，简称 CNN 或 ConvNet），而一个装满了相互独立权重的 $n \\times n$ 矩阵则是根本行不通的。\r\nCNN 的一个重大突破是这篇 NIPS 2012 论文：\r\n<span style=color:#7f8c8d;>Alex Krizhevsky、Ilya Sutskever 与 Geoffrey Hinton：ImageNet Classification with Deep Convolutional Neural Networks（用深度卷积神经网络做 ImageNet 分类）。\r\n他们的神经网络有 6000 万个参数。\r\nGraphs（图）具有另一种结构。\r\n它们由节点（nodes）以及连接这些节点的 $m$ 条边（edges）组成。\r\n这些连接由 incidence matrix（关联矩阵）来表达：$m$ 行对应边，$n$ 列对应节点。\r\n每一个图都关联着四个重要矩阵：\r\n- Incidence matrix（关联矩阵）$A$：$m \\times n$ 矩阵，每一行中有一个 $-1$ 和一个 $1$。\r\n- Adjacency matrix（邻接矩阵）$M$：$n \\times n$ 矩阵，当节点 $i$ 与节点 $j$ 相连时取 $1$。\r\n- Degree matrix（度矩阵）$D$：$n \\times n$ 对角矩阵，对角元为该行的行和。\r\n- Laplacian matrix（拉普拉斯矩阵）$L = A^{T}A = D - M$：positive semidefinite（半正定）矩阵。\r\n从深度学习的视角看，Fourier 问题与 CNN 相关联，而 graphical models（图模型）则导向 graphical nets（图网络）。\r\nGraph theory（图论）已经成为我们理解网络上离散问题的最宝贵工具。\r\n<!-- ===== PAGE BREAK ===== −->\r\n−-- OCR 原文 −--\r\npart IV ： Special Matrices\r\nThis chapter develop s two large topics ： the key matrices for Discrete Fourier Transforms\r\nand for graphical models. Both topics appear in machine learning when the problem has\r\nspecial SffUCture—whi ch is reflected in the architecture of the neural net.\r\nFouner is for probl ems with 砀 “ r 忉 巳 The operations on one pixel of an image\r\nare the s ame as the operations on th e next pixel. ln th at case the operation is a co “ 况\r\nEach row of the underlying matrix is a shift of the previous row. E ach column is a shift of\r\nthe previou s column. ConvoIutionaI nets use the same w ei ght s around e ach pixel.\r\n山 that shift-invanant structure, a convolution m atrix (a 孝 产 in image processing)\r\nhas constant diagonals · Th e by m atrix in a l-dimensional problem is fully determined\r\nby its first row and column · Very 0 n the m atrix is banded—the filter has fimte length—\r\nthe has zero s outside a band of diagonals. For 2-dimensional problem s with rep e ated\r\none-dimen sion al blocks the saving iS enormou &\r\nThis makes it possible to use a Convolutional Neural Net (CNN or ConvNet) when\r\nby 2 matrix full of independent weights would be impossible. A maJ or breakthrough\r\nsto of CNN ， s was thi s 'NIP S 2012 P ap er ：\r\nAlex Krizhevsky ， llya Sutskever, an d Geoffrey Hinton ： ImageNet CI “ s ca 五 0 视 w 氵\r\nDeep Co “ 况 Neural e ks · Their neural net h ad 60 million parameters.\r\nGraphs have a different struc ture · They consist of nodes connected by m edges.\r\nThose connections are expressed by the incidence matrix ： m row s for the edges\r\nand column s for the nodes. Every graph is associated with four important matnces ：\r\nlncidence matrix 蓋\r\nAdj acency matrix M\r\nDegree matrix D\r\nm by with 一 1 and 1 in each row\r\n1 when nodes an d j are connected\r\nby with\r\nby diagonal matrix with row sums of\r\nposiUve semidefinite matnx\r\nLaplacian matrix L = AT 蓋 = 一 M\r\nFrom the viewpoint of deep learning, Founer problemS are associated with CNN ， s and\r\nbaphlcal models le ad to graphic al nets. Graph theory has become 0 ur most valuable to 01\r\nto Understand di s crete problems on networks.\r\n203"
